# Tinybones, Bauble Burglar: "{3}{B}, {T}: Each opponent discards a card. Activate only as a sorcery" and "Whenever an opponent
# discards a card, exile it from their graveyard with a stash counter on it" (CR 701.9a, 701.13, 122.1). Bot1 casts Tinybones on
# turn 1 and on turn 3 taps Swamp, Swamp, Mox Jet and Mox Ruby, which pay it exactly, the pool empty after. Bot2 discards the Lightning Bolt (its hand a Bolt and Mountains); it sits in the graveyard
# as the trigger waits, then is exiled, not left in Bot2's graveyard. "During your turn, you may play cards you don't own with stash counters on them from
# exile, and mana of any type can be spent to cast those spells": Bot1, with only Mox Pearl's {W} open, casts the Bolt at Bot2
# for its {R}, and the Bolt, leaving exile, goes to its owner's graveyard. The Mountain Bot2 discarded to its hand size at
# the end of turn 2 was exiled with a stash counter the same way (it stays there, unplayed).

